class Solution {
public:
    string largeOddNum(string& s) {
        int start = 0, end = s.size() - 1;
        while (end >= start && ((s[end] - '0') % 2 == 0)) {
            --end;
        }
        while (start <= end && s[start] == '0') {
            ++start;
        }
        string ans = s.substr(start, end - start + 1);
        return ans;
    }
};
```

**Time Complexity:** $O(N)$

**Space Complexity:** $O(N)$

## Intuition
1. First of all we have to find a odd digit from backward direction of string and if you find it in once or on any index then you just need to terminate the loop.

2. And you have to check is there any number you got if not then it  means every elements are even.

3. Now we have to find non-zero digit from starting direction of String, if we did find at once or on any index then we have to break the loop.

4. And we have to take non-zero' digit's index value and odd digit index value for extract large odd num from string.

## Solution
```java[]
class Solution {

  public String largeOddNum(String s) {

    int ind = -1;
    int n = s.length();

    for (int i = n - 1; i >= 0; i--) {

      if ((s.charAt(i) - '0') % 2 == 1) {
        ind = i;
        break;
      }
    }

    if (ind == -1) {
      return "";
    }

    int i = 0;

    while (i < n) {

      if (s.charAt(i) != '0') {
        break;
      }

      i++;
    }

    return s.substring(i, ind + 1);
  }
}
```

